  "html": "<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><table style=\"border: 2px solid #FF6600; border-left: 12px solid #FF6600; margin: -1px 10% 0px; background-color: #fff7f2; vertical-align: middle;\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"padding: 2px 0 2px 0.5em\"><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/second-renaissance/images/4/4b/Under_contruction_icon-red.png/revision/latest?cb=20171205233522\" class=\"mw-file-description image\"><img alt=\"Under contruction icon-red\" src=\"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/second-renaissance/images/4/4b/Under_contruction_icon-red.png/revision/latest/scale-to-width-down/50?cb=20171205233522\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"50\" height=\"42\" class=\"mw-file-element\" data-image-name=\"Under contruction icon-red.png\" data-image-key=\"Under_contruction_icon-red.png\" data-relevant=\"1\" /></a></span>\n</td>\n<td style=\"padding: 0.25em 0.5em; width: 100%;\"><b>The following  page is under construction</b>.\n<p>Please do not edit or alter this article in any way while this template is active. All unauthorized edits may be reverted on the admin's discretion. Propose any changes to the comment section.\n</p>\n</td></tr></tbody></table><p><b>Generational Chaos: The Cyclical Phenomena of American History</b> is a 2071 book by Dr. Yazmin Bhattaru, expanding on her 2066 essay \"The Next American Crisis.\" In the book, Bhattaru argues that American history tends to follow cycles of economic and social-political development punctuated by crisis moments coinciding with the development of each generation.\n</p><p>Bhattaru offered several deviations from the Strauss–Howe generational theory and the Friedman generational theory, but most significantly was her thesis on how institutional cycles would last much longer as a result in the increase in human lifespans. Claiming the current cycle that began around 2020 would last 100 years, not the usual 80. And the next cycle would most likely last closer to 200 years.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Highlights\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Highlights</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Economic_Cycles\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\"><b>Economic Cycles</b></span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#National_Cycles\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\"><b>National Cycles</b></span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Predictions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\"><b>Predictions</b></span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Timing_of_generations_and_cycles\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Timing of generations and cycles</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Highlights\">Highlights</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FGenerational_Chaos%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D1&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Economic_Cycles\"><b>Economic Cycles</b></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FGenerational_Chaos%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D2&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Bhattaru held that the United States experiences an economic cycle beginning with the emergence of one generation during the height of their economic independence after establishing themselves in the workforce, usually in their 30s and 40s.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"National_Cycles\"><b>National Cycles</b></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FGenerational_Chaos%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D3&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The book's most significant contribution to sociology lied in its deviation from contemporary analysis of institutional, cultural, or as she called it, \"National cycles.\" Bhattaru concurred with previous analyses from the likes of Strauss and Friedman that historically National cycles last about 80 years beginning and ending with a generation that left their adolescence during the start of the crisis and largely died by the end. Bhattaru argued that paradigm is no longer in effect, as the average lifespan as of 2077 had been extended to 105 years. She argued that this would extend the next National Cycle at least 20 years beyond where it would normally start, and would end less as a result of the death of the Millenials, and more as a result of them being replaced as the largest generation by simple population growth.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Predictions\"><b>Predictions</b></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FGenerational_Chaos%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D4&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Bhattaru famously predicted with startling accuracy the coming <a href=\"/wiki/Second_Depression\" title=\"Second Depression\">Second Depression</a>, identifying the year it would occur, the depth of its impact on the job market, and ultimately how it would be resolved.\n</p><p>She also predicted the inevitability of the United States relationship with Mexico, however in this regard she made some notable errors, such as her claim that the US-Mexican Cold War would be punctuated by only one direct conflict between both powers, and while she correctly assessed that it would be the most destructive war in living memory, she believed the United States would loose the war after the American space colonies become independent.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Timing_of_generations_and_cycles\">Timing of generations and cycles</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Sign in to edit\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"log-in-edit-section\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://auth.fandom.com/signin?redirect=https%3A%2F%2Fsecond-renaissance.fandom.com%2Fwiki%2FGenerational_Chaos%3Fveaction%3Dedit%26section%3D5&amp;uselang=en&amp;metadata=article-registration-edit-article-section\" data-auth-modal=\"signin\" data-testid=\"log-in-edit-section\" aria-label=\"Sign in to edit\"><svg class=\"wds-icon wds-icon-tiny\" aria-hidden=\"true\" focusable=\"false\"><use xlink:href=\"#wds-icons-pencil-tiny\"></use></svg></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin-left:10ex\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>Generation</th>\n<th>Generation Archetype</th>\n<th>Generation Birth Year Span</th>\n<th>Entered childhood in a</th>\n<th>Turning Year Span\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Revolutionary Saeculum (90 years)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Awakening Generation</td>\n<td>Prophet (Idealist)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1701–1723 (23)</td>\n<td>1st Turning: High: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augustan_literature\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Augustan literature\">Augustan Age of Empire</a></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1704–1727 (23)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"new\" title=\"Liberty Generation (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTGliZXJ0eV9HZW5lcmF0aW9uP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Liberty Generation</span></td>\n<td>Nomad (Reactive)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1724–1741 (18)</td>\n<td>2nd Turning: Awakening: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Great_Awakening\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:First Great Awakening\">Great Awakening</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Enlightenment\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Age of Enlightenment\">Age of Enlightenment</a></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1727–1746 (19)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Republican_Generation\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Republican Generation\">Republican Generation</a></td>\n<td>Hero (Civic)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1742–1766 (25)</td>\n<td>3rd Turning: Unraveling: <span class=\"new\" title=\"French and Indian War (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRnJlbmNoX2FuZF9JbmRpYW5fV2FyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">French and Indian War</span>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colonialism\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Colonialism\">British Imperialism</a></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1746–1773 (27)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Pioneer Economy 1776-1828 (52 years)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Compromise Generation</td>\n<td>Artist (Adaptive)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1767–1791 (23)</td>\n<td>4th Turning: Crisis: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Revolution\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:American Revolution\">American Revolution</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Revolution\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Age of Revolution\">Age of Revolution</a></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1773–1794 (21)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Slavery Saeculum (71 years)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transcendental Generation</td>\n<td>Prophet (Idealist)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1792–1821 (28)</td>\n<td>1st Turning: High: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Era_of_Good_Feelings\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Era of Good Feelings\">Era of Good Feelings</a></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1794–1822 (28)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Yeoman Economy 1828-1876 (48 years)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gilded_Generation_(Strauss%E2%80%93Howe_theory)\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Gilded Generation (Strauss–Howe theory)\">Gilded Generation</a></td>\n<td>Nomad (Reactive)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1822–1842 (21)</td>\n<td>2nd Turning: Awakening: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_Great_Awakening\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Second Great Awakening\">Transcendental Awakening</a>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Romanticism (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUm9tYW50aWNpc20/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Romanticism</span>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Abolitionism (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQWJvbGl0aW9uaXNtP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Abolitionism</span></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1822–1844 (22)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Civil War Generation</td>\n<td>Hero (Civic)</td>\n<td></td>\n<td>3rd Turning: Unraveling: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican%E2%80%93American_War\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Mexican–American War\">Mexican War and Sectionalism</a>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Gold Rush (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvR29sZF9SdXNoP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Gold Rush</span>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Wild West (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvV2lsZF9XZXN0P2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Wild West</span></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1844–1860 (16)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Progressive_Era\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Progressive Era\">Progressive Generation</a></td>\n<td>Artist (Adaptive)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1843–1859 (17)</td>\n<td>4th Turning: Crisis: <span class=\"new\" title=\"American Civil War (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvQW1lcmljYW5fQ2l2aWxfV2FyP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">American Civil War</span></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1860–1865 (5)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Nationalism Saeculum (81 years)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Industrialization 1876-1932 (56 years)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"new\" title=\"Missionary Generation (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTWlzc2lvbmFyeV9HZW5lcmF0aW9uP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Missionary Generation</span></td>\n<td>Prophet (Idealist)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1860–1882 (23)</td>\n<td>1st Turning: High: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reconstruction_era_of_the_United_States\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Reconstruction era of the United States\">Reconstruction</a>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Gilded Age (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvR2lsZGVkX0FnZT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Gilded Age</span></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1865–1886 (21)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"new\" title=\"Lost Generation (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvTG9zdF9HZW5lcmF0aW9uP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Lost Generation</span></td>\n<td>Nomad (Reactive)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1883–1900 (18)</td>\n<td>2nd Turning: Awakening: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_Great_Awakening\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Third Great Awakening\">Missionary Awakening</a>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Progressive era (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUHJvZ3Jlc3NpdmVfZXJhP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Progressive era</span></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1886–1908 (22)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"new\" title=\"G.I. Generation (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRy5JLl9HZW5lcmF0aW9uP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">G.I. Generation</span></td>\n<td>Hero (Civic)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1901–1924 (24)</td>\n<td>3rd Turning: Unraveling: <span class=\"new\" title=\"World War I (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvV29ybGRfV2FyX0k/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">World War I</span>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prohibition_in_the_United_States\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Prohibition in the United States\">Prohibition</a>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Roaring Twenties (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUm9hcmluZ19Ud2VudGllcz9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Roaring Twenties</span></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1908–1929 (21)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Industrial Economy 1932-1980 (48 years)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"new\" title=\"Silent Generation (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvU2lsZW50X0dlbmVyYXRpb24/YWN0aW9uPWVkaXQmcmVkbGluaz0x\">Silent Generation</span></td>\n<td>Artist (Adaptive)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1925–1942 (18)</td>\n<td>4th Turning: Crisis: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Great_Depression_in_the_United_States\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Great Depression in the United States\">Great Depression</a>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"World War II (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvV29ybGRfV2FyX0lJP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">World War II</span>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Dust Bowl (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvRHVzdF9Cb3dsP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Dust Bowl</span></td>\n<td align=\"center\">1929–1946 (17)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th colspan=\"5\">Bretton Woods Saeculum (83 years)\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_boomers\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"wikipedia:Baby boomers\">Baby Boom Generation</a></td>\n<td>Prophet (Idealist)</td>\n<td align=\"center\">1943–1960 (18)</td>\n<td>1st Turning: High: <span class=\"new\" title=\"Pax Americana (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvUGF4X0FtZXJpY2FuYT9hY3Rpb249ZWRpdCZyZWRsaW5rPTE=\">Superpower America</span>, <span class=\"new\" title=\"Golden Age of Capitalism (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L